# Component Architecture

## Feature Creation Order

1. Schema → `lib/schemas/[feature].ts`
2. API Route → `app/api/[feature]/route.ts`
3. Hook → `hooks/[feature]/use[Feature]Query.ts`
4. Component → `components/[feature]/[Feature]Table.tsx`
5. Page Client → `components/[feature]/[Feature]PageClient.tsx`
6. Page → `app/(business)/[feature]/page.tsx`

## New Top-Level Pages

- Add sidebar item in `components/layouts/AppLayout/components/simple-sidebar.tsx`
- Add route metadata in `lib/utils/route-metadata.ts`
- Add to `protectedAdminRoutes` in `proxy.ts`

## API Routes

- Always check session: `auth.api.getSession({ headers: request.headers })`
- Always scope queries by `admin.business.id`
- Validate inputs with Zod schema
- Use `sanitizeErrorMessage()` from `lib/utils/error-handler.ts` for errors
- Return consistent shape: `{ items: [], total: 0, page: 1, perPage: 10, error?: string }`

## React Query Hooks

- Use `useSearchParams()` for server-side filtering
- Include queryString in queryKey: `["features", queryString]`
- Use `placeholderData: (prev) => prev` for optimistic updates

## Data Tables

- Default to server-side filtering
- Set `shallow: false` in useDataTable for URL-triggered refetches
- Use unique `queryKeys` per table to avoid URL conflicts

## Loading States

- Static content (titles, labels, descriptions) stays visible
- Only skeleton dynamic content (inputs, buttons, table rows)
- Wrap in `<Suspense fallback={<Component isLoading={true} />}>`

## Key Patterns

- Index files (`index.ts`) for clean imports
- Settings pages use `_components/` folder (underscore prefix)
- Toast for success/error feedback via `sonner`
- Never expose raw database errors to client

