## API Routes

### Standard Structure

**File:** `app/api/[feature]/route.ts`

```typescript
export async function GET(request: Request) {
  // 1. Session check
  // 2. Business context (admin.business.id)
  // 3. Parse & validate query params (Zod)
  // 4. Build where clause (ALWAYS scope by businessId)
  // 5. Build orderBy
  // 6. Execute queries (Promise.all for count + data)
  // 7. Format & return response
}
```

### Response Shape (Consistent)

```typescript
// Success
{ items: [...], total: number, page: number, perPage: number }

// Error (always include empty data)
{ error: "message", items: [], total: 0, perPage: 10 }
```

### Error Handling

**File:** `lib/utils/error-handler.ts`

- `sanitizeErrorMessage(error)` - Prevents exposing DB/internal errors
- `handleApiError(response)` - Extracts user-friendly message from response

**Never send raw database errors to client.**

