## Data Tables (Server-Side Filtering)

**Default:** Always server-side filtering unless explicitly told otherwise.

### useDataTable Configuration

```typescript
const { table } = useDataTable({
  data: displayItems,
  columns,
  pageCount: Math.ceil(total / perPage),
  shallow: false, // CRITICAL: triggers URL changes to refetch
  initialState: {
    pagination: { pageIndex: 0, pageSize: perPage },
    sorting: [{ id: "createdAt", desc: true }],
    columnPinning: { right: ["actions"] },
  },
  queryKeys: {
    // Unique per table to avoid URL conflicts
    page: "featurePage",
    perPage: "featurePerPage",
    sort: "featureSort",
    filters: "featureFilters",
  },
});
```

### Column Meta for Filters

```typescript
meta: {
  label: "Name",
  variant: "text",        // text | number | range | date | dateRange | select | multiSelect
  placeholder: "Filter...",
  maxLength: 255,         // Client-side limit
  options: [],            // For select variants
}
```

### Skeleton Rows Pattern

```typescript
const displayItems = useMemo(() => {
  if (isLoading && items.length === 0) {
    return Array.from({ length: perPage }, (_, i) => ({
      id: `skeleton-${i}`,
      // ... empty fields
    }));
  }
  if (!isLoading && items.length === 0) {
    return [{ id: "empty-state", ... }];
  }
  return items;
}, [items, isLoading, perPage]);

// In cell renderer
if (item.id.startsWith("skeleton-")) return <Skeleton className="h-4 w-32" />;
```

